# Real-Time Chat Backend

A real-time one-to-one chat backend built with **NestJS**, **MongoDB**, **Mongoose**, and **Socket.IO**.

The application provides:

* User registration and authentication
* JWT access and refresh tokens
* User search
* One-to-one conversations
* Real-time messaging
* Message delivery status
* Online status
* Typing indicators
* Conversation management
* Email sending through Gmail SMTP

---

# 1. Setup

## Requirements

Before running the project, make sure you have:

* Node.js
* npm
* MongoDB
* Git
* Docker (optional)

---

# 2. Install Dependencies

Clone the project:

```bash
git clone <repository-url>
cd <project-folder>
```

Install the backend dependencies:

```bash
npm install
```

---

# 3. Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the project root.

Example:

```env
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://mongodb:27017/chat

DOMAIN=http://localhost:3000
PORT=3000

MAIL_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
MAIL_PORT=587
MAIL_USER=your-email@gmail.com
MAIL_PASS=your-gmail-app-password
MAIL_FROM=your-email@gmail.com

ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET=your_access_token_secret
ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRES_IN=1d

REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET=your_refresh_token_secret
REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRES_IN=7d

NODE_ENV=development

SERVER_MODE=local

FRONTEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5500/
```

## Environment Variables

| Variable                   | Description                                 | Example                        |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| `MONGODB_URI`              | MongoDB connection string                   | `mongodb://mongodb:27017/chat` |
| `DOMAIN`                   | Backend application domain                  | `http://localhost:3000`        |
| `PORT`                     | Port used by the backend                    | `3000`                         |
| `MAIL_HOST`                | Gmail SMTP server                           | `smtp.gmail.com`               |
| `MAIL_PORT`                | Gmail SMTP port                             | `587`                          |
| `MAIL_USER`                | Gmail account used to send emails           | `your-email@gmail.com`         |
| `MAIL_PASS`                | Gmail App Password                          | `your-gmail-app-password`      |
| `MAIL_FROM`                | Sender email address                        | `your-email@gmail.com`         |
| `ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET`      | Secret used to sign access JWTs             | `your_access_token_secret`     |
| `ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRES_IN`  | Access token lifetime                       | `1d`                           |
| `REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET`     | Secret used to sign refresh JWTs            | `your_refresh_token_secret`    |
| `REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRES_IN` | Refresh token lifetime                      | `7d`                           |
| `NODE_ENV`                 | Application environment                     | `development`                  |
| `SERVER_MODE`              | Server/network configuration mode           | `local`                        |
| `FRONTEND_URL`             | URL allowed to communicate with the backend | `http://127.0.0.1:5500/`       |

---

# 4. Email Configuration

The application uses **Gmail SMTP** to send emails.

No external email delivery service such as SendGrid, Mailgun, or Amazon SES is required.

Emails are sent through a Gmail account using Gmail's SMTP server.

## Gmail SMTP Settings

```env
MAIL_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
MAIL_PORT=587
MAIL_USER=your-email@gmail.com
MAIL_PASS=your-gmail-app-password
MAIL_FROM=your-email@gmail.com
```

## Gmail App Password

The application uses a **Gmail App Password** for SMTP authentication instead of the normal Gmail account password.

The Gmail account must have **2-Step Verification** enabled before an App Password can be created.

The generated App Password should be placed in:

```env
MAIL_PASS=your-gmail-app-password
```

The normal Gmail account password should not be used or stored in the application.

## Security

Email credentials and JWT secrets are sensitive and must not be committed to Git.

Add the following to `.gitignore`:

```gitignore
.env
```

Never commit:

```text
MAIL_PASS
ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET
REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET
```

to a public repository.

---

